  "claims_to_verify": [
    "getDamage returns combatTalentSpellDamage(t, 20, 140), whose value scales with spellpower and talent level and therefore with Magic-derived spellpower.",
    "The action passes getDamage through spellCrit and projects the resulting scalar once to one hit target as DamageType.FIRE; it does not invoke FIREBURN or create BURNING duration or per-turn damage.",
    "The info path passes the uncritted getDamage scalar through damDesc(self, DamageType.FIREBURN, damage) into the one %0.2f placeholder.",
    "FIREBURN has no damdesc_split field, so damDesc does not invoke its projector, split the scalar, divide it across three turns, or establish any DoT semantics.",
    "Because damDesc queries combatGetDamageIncrease for FIREBURN rather than FIRE, the displayed scalar may omit FIRE-specific damage increase that applies to the action; this is an upstream tooltip/display inconsistency, not a translation defect.",
    "The English and Chinese each claim only flame damage plus Magic scaling and contain no duration, total-over-time, per-turn, or burning-effect claim.",
    "The exact source, target, tformat tag, null args/special, one %0.2f, one newline, and two-tab continuation remain byte-identical because the adjudicated decision is no-change."
